[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: One card per grammar element; the declaration in the side pane

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-GRAMMARS-VIEW
TITLE: One card per grammar element; the declaration in the side pane
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The Grammars view draws one uniform card per grammar element on a grid --
tag, UID prefix, and field/role/node counts -- and puts the full declaration
in the right-hand pane on selection: every field with its kind, choice words
and required flag, and every relation role the element may write. Data is the
snapshot's grammar key (parsed from grammar.sgra, since the JSON export types
every field as String); an element with zero nodes still gets a card, which
is how an empty vocabulary such as COMMENTARY stays visible. The Board
inspector's type name links here: clicking it switches the view and selects
that element's card. The switcher order is Perspective, Grammars, Board.
<<<
